 4. ⚓️ 1 for the road: Storm turns up shipwreck 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Exposed shipwreck remains along the southern shore of Nantucket, Mass. Photo: Jason Graziadei/Nantucket Current via AP Maritime experts in Nantucket are inspecting weathered wooden beams exposed by last weekend's powerful nor'easter — possibly the remnants of a 19th-century shipwreck.

 The Egan Maritime Institute is surveying the site and working with state archaeologists to determine the wreckage's origins. 🌊 The splintered timbers, fastened together by rusted iron, emerged near an area where remains believed to be from the Warren Sawyer have been found before.

 That ship ran aground in 1884 while carrying cotton and scrap iron from New Orleans to Boston. Go deeper . 

 
 
